#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:5
#: baefcbe96805461483a10ef26ec252f2
msgid "Auto Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:7
#: 3bb7481a05454143a3449aa988a7013b
msgid "In Auto mode the vehicle will follow a pre-programmed mission stored in the autopilot which is made up of navigation commands (i.e. waypoints) and “do” commands (i.e. commands that do not affect the location of the vehicle including triggering a camera shutter)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:9
#: 903d65f950ee4248a78580c61ae55843
msgid "This mode requires the vehicle have :ref:`GPS <common-positioning-landing-page>` and/or :ref:`visual odometry <common-zed>` or :ref:`wheel encoders <wheel-encoder>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:12
#: cfc00917d6d04c76b4626d404c415a8a
msgid "Creating a Mission"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:14
#: b7daa992263241379898c8358f4a8987
msgid "Most ground stations are capable of creating and uploading missions.  Mission Planner allows this using the Flight Planner screen:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:16
#: 0d4625b518db477683a8a1b9ecc6ba1d
msgid "connect your autopilot to your PC using a USB cable or telemetry"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:17
#: d23f6979afc2403abd1c801982d76812
msgid "open the Mission Planner on your PC and press the Connect button"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:18
#: 9514831822f34e1caf32434fe8ba332b
msgid "go to the Flight Planer screen and click on the map in a few places to add waypoints"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:19
#: f3192a1236fe425687bf9ce6ffceef91
msgid "in the command list section, click once on the last waypoint command in the list and press the \"Add Below\" button, a new command WAYPOINT command should appear at the bottom of the list"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:20
#: 71cb95b8b1e642fca861e1c29288e120
msgid "click on the word WAYPOINT and change the command to \"RETURN_TO_LAUNCH\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:21
#: 874bdafeb8c245c687b6dff9ce421458
msgid "upload the mission to the autopilot using the \"Write WPs\" button."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:27
#: 9e09e54c0a2e429e9673b1dd7ce9920a
msgid "Starting the Mission"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:29
#: 33b7ac2ad13a48fabc9e9b7a19799d7a
msgid "The following instructions should be followed to start the mission:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:31
#: 6cb9ece970dd47da94479df0527e79c8
msgid "setup the :ref:`transmitter mode switch <common-rc-transmitter-flight-mode-configuration>` so that Auto can be selected"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:32
#: 39bb05c25d3b4ca392874d0aa96962b9
msgid "take the vehicle outside, power it on and wait for a good position estimate (LED will turn green)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:33
#: aa404956fcbe4264a1346cb69b08ecbb
msgid "arm the vehicle in :ref:`MANUAL <manual-mode>` or :ref:`HOLD <hold-mode>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:34
#: ae7e986e9dfb4b3abc37eff88815b417
msgid "change the mode to AUTO and the vehicle should begin executing the commands one after another"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:35
#: c61b7e167e174755830099caa9d843df
msgid "if telemetry is connected you should see the vehicle travelling around the course"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:36
#: a3be0f529e0f4007987ca72c03393727
msgid "if you notice any odd behaviour, use the transmitter's mode switch at any time to change back to :ref:`MANUAL <manual-mode>` or :ref:`HOLD <hold-mode>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:37
#: 2d93f0f2f0bc4810bd37b3864c9c1d0c
msgid "if all goes well the vehicle will travel the course and then return to the point where it was armed (assuming the final command was Return-To-Launch)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:40
#: 40bbd97587bd4ce1bb135400b1f00afb
msgid "Starting the Mission with a Kick"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:42
#: e4eadde6240c4ab2840fa1e71b6f3dd5
msgid "The mission normally starts the moment the vehicle is switched into Auto mode but alternatively it can be configured to wait for an push by setting the :ref:`AUTO_KICKSTART <AUTO_KICKSTART>` parameter to an acceleration in m/s/s.  A value of 2 m/s/s will normally work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:45
#: 2cde0e612fbf4b408009b4ac6ae84044
msgid "Starting the Mission from a button"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:47
#: 363fc7f054e94a7ab92ac4627b6859a9
msgid "The mission can be started from a switch as described on the :ref:`Start/Stop switch <startstop-switch>` page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:50
#: 3ba15feac99a4827997226cbdaf045d9
msgid "Speed Nudging"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:52
#: c19e8bc857b2453c99cbe5b2d053d998
msgid "While the vehicle is executing a mission, the user can increase the vehicle's speed by raising the transmitter's throttle stick to between 75% and 100%.  At 75% the vehicle will remain at it's configured speed (i.e. :ref:`WP_SPEED <WP_SPEED>`), this linearly increases to the vehicle's maximum speed as the pilot's throttle stick reaches 100%."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:55
#: 995444d39bc748c59885be03a1507964
msgid "Mission End"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:57
#: e1f6a80eac4d48c58039803e6efad366
msgid "If a mission ends on a waypoint, then it will switch to a mode determined by the :ref:`MIS_DONE_BEHAVE<MIS_DONE_BEHAVE>` parameter. It can be changed from this mode either by the RC mode switch changing, or via ground control station."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:60
#: 30479deba692470b834a82b914b39be8
msgid "Resuming or Restarting a Mission"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:62
#: 33aeb37077c24e60b752ca976d18cdea
msgid "If a mission is interrupted (for example if the user switches the vehicle out of Auto mode before it has completed the mission) the last command executed is stored and when the vehicle is next returned to Auto mode it will resume the mission from this command.  Note: disarming the vehicle or rebooting the autopilot will reset the mission back to the first command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:64
#: 62ec46fa83904053bbea19b3668ff1e0
msgid "If you would prefer the mission was always restarted from the beginning, set the :ref:`MIS_RESTART <MIS_RESTART>` parameter to \"1\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:67
#: 1b024e01fd9b401a879dfac4ec98a78c
msgid "Setting the active command"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:69
#: 61ce70f01b364e368716bf44c90f8c89
msgid "While the vehicle is executing a mission in Auto, the active command can be changed from the ground station.  If using Mission Planner this is done from the Flight Data >> Actions tab's \"Set WP\" button."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:75
#: 757cdf158cdd4751a7f5b8930036a6cb
msgid "Tuning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/auto-mode.rst:77
#: bf6c2c8ff9ef4703af2adc7e1f8eb6d5
msgid "Details on how to tune the controllers for good waypoint control can be found on the :ref:`Tuning Navigation <rover-tuning-navigation>` page."
msgstr ""
